{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>From before the face of the dead.</b> According to the statement of Amram, of blessed memory (Shabbat 152b), that before the covering-stone is sealed, a person's soul sees and knows everything before it. Further, from here it is derived that they lay the deceased upon it (Bava Batra 64a)." "<b>And he spoke to the children of Heth, saying.</b> It intends that since he asked ״give me a possession״ etc., which from his words appears that he would be satisfied with any place they give him, therefore the verse says <b>saying</b> — meaning: this is not the purpose of the speech, but a preamble to say what he actually seeks, namely that it is this field of Ephron." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to give a reason why Abraham needed to speak to the children of Heth, and also to elaborate everything stated in the matter — for would someone who needed to acquire a burial-plot or one field to plow or to plant need to make the whole world and its inhabitants tremble? Therefore he concluded <b>saying</b> — meaning: it was not for the need of four cubits of ground to bury Sarah that he needed to speak to the inhabitants of the land, but to say what is stated in the matter — that he purchased the Cave of Machpelah, which has nothing comparable to it. And for this reason he needed to speak to all of them and to all those present, so that the purchase would be effective according to law." "<b>Further,</b> it intends to remove a great protest from upon Abraham, namely how he could ask for a free gift and say ״give me a possession.״ For this reason he prefaced and said <b>saying</b> — meaning: his heart did not think so, but from his mouth he said these things, and his intent was to come with a claim, as I shall explain nearby."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:50.983055458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}